thers, 1936","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"30 x 16 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"The long, narrow form of a tan mule's skull sits against a white surface. Two black and brown striped turkey feathers with white tips poke out from behind the skull, one at the bottom right and the other at the top left.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. Mule's Skull with Turkey Feathers, 1936. Oil on canvas, 30 x 16 inches. Private Collection. © Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Private Collection","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"(The Downtown Gallery, New York, NY); Private collection, Greenwich, Connecticut, 1952; Private collection, Santa Fe, New Mexico, purchase, after 1966; Gerald Peters Gallery, Santa Fe, New Mexico, 1986; Private collection, Dallas, Texas, 1988; (Gerald Peters Gallery, Santa Fe, New Mexico) (Source: Lynes, 1999)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Abiquiú Notebooks notes inscription 1. Abiquiú Notebooks after 1977 notes, \"Sold by Halpert . . . April 1952.\" (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classif